Changes with the nginx-autocert-module 1.3.0                     10 Aug 2026

    *) License: the module is now BSD-2-Clause, matching nginx and angie. It
       was previously distributed under different terms; redistributors should
       read the new LICENSE file rather than assuming the old one carries over.

    *) Feature: autocert_ca_issuance_certificate verifies the issued chain
       against a trust anchor before it can replace the live certificate,
       as defence in depth against a buggy or compromised CA. Opt-in: unset
       (the default) keeps the previous behaviour. It is deliberately NOT
       autocert_ca_trusted_certificate — that anchors the CA's TLS endpoint,
       and a CA may sign certificates under a different root than it serves
       its API under, in which case reusing it rejects every issuance. The
       anchor may be the CA's root or its issuing intermediate.

    *) Feature: a runtime certificate-issuance API for other nginx modules. A
       named shared-memory zone (autocert_requests) lets a separate module ask
       for ACME certificates at runtime; autocert orders, renews, persists and
       serves them. Inert unless a consumer module attaches to the zone. See
       docs/API.md.

    *) Feature: runtime issuance is provisioned by "autocert on" rather than by
       the number of configured names. A label-driven gateway matching hosts
       with a regex or catch-all server_name contributes zero issuable names at
       config time, so the requests zone, the challenge zone with its :80
       HTTP-01 handler, and the ACME account were all silently never created.

    *) Feature: a cert_cb delegation hook for consumer modules. OpenSSL keeps
       exactly one cert_cb per SSL_CTX and offers no getter to chain through, so
       a second module installing its own cert_cb silently broke autocert's
       serving: certificates still issued and landed in the store, but every
       name was served the self-signed bootstrap certificate with nothing
       logged.

    *) Feature: idle-TTL garbage collection for the runtime registry (shm API
       v2). The registry is a bounded 64-node table; a host learned at runtime
       was never evicted, so a long-lived gateway churning more than 64 distinct
       hosts wedged at the cap permanently.

    *) Bugfix: an ordinary "nginx -s reload" discarded the shared-memory tree in
       all three zones (requests, challenge, alpn). nginx's zone-reuse path
       calls init() without setting shm.exists, which on Linux is always 0, so
       every reload re-allocated the zone header and orphaned the rbtree.

    *) Bugfix: a pre-planted FIFO at <store>/<seg>/.autocert-runtime wedged
       worker 0 indefinitely. O_NOFOLLOW rejects a symlink but not a FIFO, and
       opening a FIFO for writing blocks until a reader appears, stalling the
       sole ACME driver event loop right after a successful runtime issuance.

    *) Bugfix: IP literals are rejected on the runtime request path. IP
       certificates (RFC 8738) are config-driven, but a dotted-quad is
       LDH-clean, so an IPv4 literal passed the charset gate and would reach a
       real ACME order.

    *) Bugfix: activity stamping no longer discards the shared-memory layout
       identity.

    *) Bugfix: a runtime request left PENDING by a lost order completion is now
       aged out by the idle-TTL GC instead of being skipped forever. Disabling
       autocert while an order was in flight could strand that hostname until a
       full restart, because a reload reuses the shared-memory zone.

    *) Change: the module now fails to start when nginx is built without SSL
       support, instead of failing later at first use.

    *) CI standardisation against nginx-skeleton-module. All CI material moved
       under ci/, and ci.yml became the single pull_request entry point: the
       other workflows are workflow_call members, so a PR asks for one run
       rather than several independent ones. Members keep their push: and
       schedule: triggers for direct coverage of master.

    *) Ported the ci/linter framework and wired lint.yml into the suite: the
       same lint-*.sh checkers run in the pre-commit hook and on the PR, so
       local green predicts remote green instead of merely correlating with
       it. The blocking set (LINT_ONLY) is a deliberate subset; a checker
       joins it in the same change that makes it green, so the gate only
       ratchets forward.

    *) Added ci/linter/lint-python.sh. ci/linter/workflow_policy.py implements
       the rule for five of the eleven checkers and had no checker of its own.
       Rules are selected explicitly because ruff's default set omits F401 and
       E402 -- a stray unused import passed a bare `ruff check`.

    *) Added ci/tools/ci-build.sh as the single chokepoint for building nginx
       plus the module, and adopted it in codeql.yml, security-scanners.yml
       and ci-deep.yml.

    *) Added a coverage build profile and ci/tools/coverage.sh, and verified
       the coverage filter actually moves rather than reporting a constant.

    *) Added a fuzz target for the base64url decode wrapper, a drift gate
       holding fuzz.dict against the parser's literals, and a replay of every
       past crash on each PR. fuzzing.yml had become orphaned from the merge
       path and was reconnected; reconnecting it exposed and fixed a stale
       corpus path.

    *) Added an ASan/UBSan soak workflow (asan.yml) on a weekly schedule, and
       fixed the two non-defects that had kept it red since it was written.
       The soak now detects a sanitizer report wherever it lands: a
       sanitizer's log_path is not a contract, and GCC's UBSan wrote its
       report into nginx's error.log rather than the configured path.

    *) Added a sync-stamp gate over the .github/ files shared with the
       skeleton, so an adopter can diff two repos and see exactly what
       drifted.

    *) Added workflow-policy checks for runner selection, port bands, trigger
       cadence and secret declarations, each with fixture trees that must go
       red.

    *) Wired ccache into the nginx configure step. It had been installed and
       configured but was never reaching the compiler, so the cache recorded
       no hits at all.

    *) Fixed a NULL-log segfault reached through the crypto unit tests, and
       closed mutation-testing gaps at the length, depth and overflow
       boundaries. A year-9999 boundary assertion compared two implementations
       that both return (time_t) -1 on a narrow time_t, so it could not fail;
       it now requires a representable reference.

    *) Scoped e2e container reaping by GITHUB_RUN_ID so concurrent jobs cannot
       kill each other's containers, and derived e2e port bands from the run
       ID with the ceiling verified before anything binds.

    *) CONTRIBUTING.md now tells a contributor to enable the pre-commit hook,
       which is what makes the local and remote gates agree.


Changes with the nginx-autocert-module 1.2.0                     11 Jul 2026

    *) See the git history and the GitHub release notes for v1.2.0 and
       earlier. This file starts at the CI standardisation above; it was not
       maintained for the releases that precede it.
